  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224903/assets/c8f6d0161777412704a9a80c0336af04a6968454d421913055024b6d0cf11c71.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224903/assets/b50fd1636cc2e1bb9d150eaba9cc25a3ccedff77e607bf22853004332a7c4ddc.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(3,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(5,3).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{2} \\\\  & =-1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
